R20 — the per-eye lighting split: the headset's frustum, injectable on a simulator,
and the instruments that name the channel it acts through.

EVERYTHING IN THIS PATCH IS OFF BY DEFAULT and inert in a shipped frame:

  gl_vrtan0 / gl_vrtan1   empty      inject a per-eye frustum (the Vision Pro's own
                                     tangents, which a visionOS SIMULATOR never reports)
  gl_vrtancull            0          apply the injection to the CULLING frustum only, so
                                     the two eye images stay pixel-comparable
  gl_batchshots           0          print the next N renders' per-batch light sets
  gl_dlight_batchkey      0          CANDIDATE (not a fix): put the face's light set in the
                                     batch key so shading is per-face and view-independent

and three prints that only appear under gl_lightdiag / gl_batchshots:
  DRAWDIAG ... batches= ubits= tan=   the batch side of 0043, plus the frustum used
  PPLBATCH / PPLUBO / FACEBITS        the batch union, the UBO bytes, and every drawn
                                      face's bits — the three places a per-eye lighting
                                      difference can be born

Measurements, controls and conclusions: artifacts/vr-r20/DIAG-per-eye-spot.md

